      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "DyCl3·6H2O (0.0386 g, 0.1 mmol) and 2-methyl-2-((2'-hydroxynaphthalen-1'-yl)methyleneamino)propanediol (0.0259 g, 0.1 mmol) were placed in a Pyrex tube with ethanol (1 mL), acetonitrile (1 mL), and triethylamine (30 μL). The tube was sealed under vacuum and heated in an oven at 80 °C for 3 days. Slow cooling afforded light yellow crystals of 1. Yield 19% based on DyCl3·6H2O. The authors note crystal formation requires at least ~60 °C, with ~80 °C optimum, and that sole ethanol or acetonitrile or routine solution methods failed.",
